        body: "This guide solves: maximise z = x + 2y subject to x + y <= 5, x + 3y <= 9 and x, y >= 0.\n\nStart with a new chart. Click + Add and choose Feasible region (inequalities). The card R1 arrives with the two sign conditions `x >= 0` and `y >= 0` filled in, an empty third row, and the chip Constraint lines switched on.",
