        body: "On the card R1 click Add condition and type the first row below. Then type CS into the field Label.\n\nThe new row cuts the triangle at the equilibrium price. What remains lies above the price and below demand: the consumer surplus, what buyers were willing to pay beyond the price.",
        type: [
          { where: "R1, condition 2", text: "y >= P1_y" },
          { where: "R1, Label", text: "CS" }
        ],
        chart: chart2(__spreadProps(__spreadValues({}, axes), { functions: [demand, supply], tools: [withDropLines, consumer] })),
        shot: {
          reveal: ["R1"],
          actions: [{ focus: ["R1", "condition:1"] }],
          caption: "One more row: above the equilibrium price P1_y."
        },
        tip: "A computed value in a condition needs no brackets or braces: write `P1_y` like any other name."
